# 🚀 Ultimate Markdown Stress Test

> If your Markdown renderer survives this file, it's production-ready.

---

## 1. Headings (All Levels)

# H1 — Title Level  
## H2 — Section Level  
### H3 — Subsection  
#### H4 — Minor Section  
##### H5 — Small Section  
###### H6 — Tiny Section  

---

## 2. Text Formatting

**Bold Text**  
*Italic Text*  
***Bold + Italic***  
~~Strikethrough~~  
<u>Underline (HTML)</u>  

Inline `code snippet` inside a paragraph.

---

## 3. Horizontal Rule

---
***
___

---

## 4. Lists

### Unordered

- Item 1
  - Sub Item 1.1
    - Sub Sub Item 1.1.1
- Item 2
- Item 3

### Ordered

1. First
2. Second
   1. Second.1
   2. Second.2
3. Third

### Task List

- [x] Completed Task
- [ ] Pending Task
- [ ] Another Task

---

## 5. Links

[OpenAI](https://openai.com)  
<https://github.com>

Reference-style link:

[Google][google]

[google]: https://google.com

---

## 6. Blockquotes

> This is a blockquote  
>> Nested blockquote  
>>> Triple nested

---

## 7. Code Blocks

### JavaScript

```javascript
function fibonacci(n) {
  if (n <= 1) return n;
  return fibonacci(n - 1) + fibonacci(n - 2);
}
console.log(fibonacci(10));
```

### Python

```python
class Agent:
    def __init__(self, name):
        self.name = name

    def speak(self):
        return f"Hello, I am {self.name}"

agent = Agent("AI")
print(agent.speak())
```

### Bash

```bash
#!/bin/bash
echo "Markdown Viewer Test"
ls -la
```

---

## 8. Tables

| Feature        | Supported | Notes |
|---------------|----------|-------|
| Headings      | ✅        | All 6 |
| Tables        | ✅        | Styled |
| Code Blocks   | ✅        | Highlighted |
| Footnotes     | ❓        | Check |

Alignment test:

| Left | Center | Right |
|:-----|:------:|------:|
| A    | B      | C     |
| 1    | 2      | 3     |

